## State Model

### `Room` (backend, in-memory)

```typescript
interface Room {
  code: string;                    // Unique 4-char alphanumeric (auto-generated)
  status: "lobby" | "playing" | "result";  // S4 adds "result"
  hostId: string;                  // Participant ID of room creator (S1)
  drawerId: string;                // Current drawer's participant ID (S2)
  secretWord: string;              // Current round's secret word (S2)
  round: number;                   // Current round number (S2)
  participants: Participant[];     // All joined players
  guesses: Guess[];                // Round guess history (S3)
  scores: Record<string, number>;  // participantId → score (S3)
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

### `RoomSnapshot` (returned to clients)

```typescript
interface RoomSnapshot {
  code: string;
  status: "lobby" | "playing" | "result";
  hostId: string;
  drawerId: string;
  secretWord?: string;        // Only present if viewer is drawer (S2)
  round: number;
  participants: Participant[];
  guesses: Guess[];           // Full guess history (S3)
  scores: Record<string, number>;  // S3
  correctWord?: string;       // Revealed in result state (S4)
  availableWords: string[];
  roles: ParticipantRole[];
}
```

### `Guess` (S3)

```typescript
interface Guess {
  participantId: string;
  playerName: string;
  text: string;
  isCorrect: boolean;
  timestamp: string;
}
```

---

## Data Flow

### Scenario 1 (Implemented)

```
Create Room:
  POST /rooms { playerName }
    → createRoom() generates code, sets hostId = participant.id
    → 201 { participantId, room: RoomSnapshot }

Join Room:
  POST /rooms/:code/join { playerName }
    → joinRoom() validates code exists, adds participant
    → 200 { participantId, room: RoomSnapshot }

Poll Lobby:
  GET /rooms/:code?participantId=X
    → getRoom() returns fresh snapshot
    → Frontend polls every 2s, updates participant list

Start Game:
  POST /rooms/:code/start { participantId }
    → startGame() validates host + ≥2 players
    → Sets drawerId, secretWord, round, status="playing"
    → 200 { room: RoomSnapshot }
```

### Scenario 2 (Implemented)

```
Name Validation:
  Zod .trim().min(1) on createRoomSchema & joinRoomSchema
  Frontend also trims and rejects empty before submit

Drawer Assignment:
  startGame() sets drawerId = hostId

Word Selection:
  selectWord(code) = STARTER_WORDS[sum(charCodes) % 5]

Snapshot Gating:
  toRoomSnapshot(room, viewerId):
    secretWord = (viewerId === room.drawerId) ? room.secretWord : undefined
```

### Scenario 3 (Planned)

```
Submit Guess:
  POST /rooms/:code/guess { participantId, text }
    → Trim text, reject if empty
    → Case-insensitive compare to room.secretWord
    → Add Guess { participantId, text, isCorrect, timestamp }
    → If correct, award 100 points to guesser
    → Return updated room snapshot

Fetch State (polling):
  GET /rooms/:code?participantId=X
    → Returns snapshot with guesses[], scores {}

Canvas Drawing:
  Client-side only in React canvas element
  Drawer can draw strokes and clear canvas
  (Out of scope: real-time sync to guessers)
```

### Scenario 4 (Planned)

```
End Round:
  POST /rooms/:code/end-round (or triggered by correct guess)
    → Set status = "result"
    → Reveal correctWord to all (in snapshot)

Restart:
  POST /rooms/:code/restart { participantId }
    → Validate participant is host (403 if not)
    → Reset: drawerId="", secretWord="", round=0, guesses=[], scores={}
    → Set status = "lobby"
    → Participants preserved
    → 200 { room: RoomSnapshot with status="lobby" }
```

